{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792961500,"nonce":"aqm1G5/adNgz1wRxqQlQXj+/SZo=","message":"Local implementation is Rust under web/cloud (Workers WASM and SQLite-backed account/workspace Durable Objects). The uncommitted JavaScript backend prototype was removed. Node dependencies are build/test tools and mocks only; browser-side JavaScript remains the host adapter.\n\nImplemented GitHub App OAuth with cookie-bound one-use state and PKCE, refreshable server-held user tokens, repository installation pagination, CSRF, account expiry/logout, repository access checks, owner-scoped stable workspace IDs, asynchronous idempotent provisioning/retry, persisted workspace metadata, and an authenticated WebSocket gateway. The compute credential stays private and is injected into hello at the gateway. Logout disconnects that account's sockets. Browser Open Project/Folder now uses a repository chooser with sign-in, filtering, bounded mounted rows, pagination and startup progress. Anonymous startup opens Welcome with Explorer collapsed; the local sample requires demo=1.\n\nVerification: all 6 Rust Worker integration tests pass in local workerd, including persistence across a Durable Object restart, token refresh, provisioning retry, cross-account rejection and real Rust workspace reads/logout. The full Chrome flow passed sign-in (mock GitHub), repository selection, connection to a real Rust session server, and reload without reprovisioning. Browser CRDT client tests: 9 passed. Artifacts: bin/cloud-final-checks.log, bin/cloud-browser-flow.log and bin/web/github-flow/.\n\nImportant scope boundary: GitHub and compute provisioning are mocked in these local tests. No service was deployed. A real GitHub App/secrets, a trusted production sandbox provisioner (including checkout/credential containment), active-access revocation, usage policy, Durable Object document authority and full editor CRDT binding remain open. The provider contract and setup instructions are in web/cloud/README.md. The already tested MSB runtime on the NUC is not yet a production provider.","files":null}]}